*** ch14-01-nat-variant — non-FVP addition theory: incremental variant generation and incremental variant unification (Maude manual §14.2, §14.6, §14.11)

fmod NAT-VARIANT is
 sort Nat .
 op 0 : -> Nat [ctor] .
 op s : Nat -> Nat [ctor] .
 op _+_ : Nat Nat -> Nat .
 vars X Y : Nat .
 eq [base] : 0 + Y = Y [variant] .
 eq [ind]  : s(X) + Y = s(X + Y) [variant] .
endfm

*** §14.6: finite set of most general variants (1 variant) despite non-FVP theory
get variants in NAT-VARIANT : s(0) + X:Nat .

*** §14.6: bounded approximation of an infinite set of most general variants (10 variants)
get variants [10] in NAT-VARIANT : X:Nat + s(0) .

*** §14.11: one unifier, terminates with "No more unifiers."
variant unify in NAT-VARIANT : s(0) + X:Nat =? s(s(s(0)))  .

*** §14.11: bound [1] required — without it Maude would not stop
variant unify [1] in NAT-VARIANT : X:Nat + s(0) =? s(s(s(0)))  .
